PN,11804
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Foreign Office in London says it
OL,6, now believes a British passport holder
OL,7, on board the Pan Am jet in the Karachi
OL,8, airport siege was killed.
OL,10,FTwo Britons are reported to have been
OL,11,Fwounded in shooting at the end of the
OL,12,F17-hour siege, while 20 escaped unhurt.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FEighteen people died and more than 120
OL,15,Fpeople were injured during the
OL,16,Fhijacking.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe four Arabic-speaking gunmen opened
OL,19,Ffire on the 389 passengers when the
OL,20,Flights went out. One of the hijackers
OL,21,Fwas killed and three are in custody.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     GG5/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A Pakistani aviation official has
OL,6, denied that there was a pre-arranged
OL,7, plan to storm the hijacked Pan Am jet
OL,8, at Karachi airport.
OL,10,FHe said a failure of a generator -
OL,11,Fpredicted hours before - led to a loss
OL,12,Fof lights. The terrorists then panicked
OL,13,Fand started to shoot their hostages.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FOnly then did commandos move in and
OL,16,Fthen not for many minutes. "We didn't
OL,17,Fwant to storm the plane. We were just
OL,18,Freacting to events," he said.
OL,20,FThe official, head of Pakistan's civil
OL,21,Faviation authority, denied he was
OL,22,Fcontradicting an earlier report that
OL,23,Fthe operation went as planned.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The director of Pakistan's civil
OL,6, aviation authority has contradicted
OL,7, his earlier story that the attack on
OL,8, the hijacked Pan Am jet at Karachi
OL,9, Airport was a planned affair.
OL,11,FHe said army commandos did not come
OL,12,Fnear the plane for about 15 minutes
OL,13,Fafter the hijackers began to shoot at
OL,14,Fthe hostages on board.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FHe also said there was "never
OL,17,Factually a storming of the plane" and
OL,18,Fsaid the hijackers had half an hour's
OL,19,Fwarning that the lights would fail.
OL,21,FThe director also said that only one
OL,22,Fhijacker had been killed, not two as
OL,23,Foriginally reported.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The United States has congratulated the
OL,6, authorities in Pakistan for their
OL,7, storming of the hijacked plane.
OL,9,FA statement issued by President Reagan
OL,10,Fsaid it had been bold and decisive,
OL,11,Fin contrast to the hijack itself,
OL,12,Fwhich he described as "despicable and
OL,13,Fcowardly".
OL,14,F
OL,15,F"We can think of no punishment too
OL,16,Fsevere for the criminals responsible"
OL,17,Fsaid President Reagan, adding that he
OL,18,Fwas sure they would be brought to
OL,19,Fjustice.
OL,20,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Some of the Britons on board the plane
OL,6, involved in a siege at Karachi airport
OL,7, have been talking about their ordeal.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FOne of them, Mr Mike Thexton, said that
OL,10,Fafter the aircraft's lights went out,
OL,11,Fthe terrorists panicked and began
OL,12,Ffiring at random.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FOther passengers said they sheltered
OL,15,Ffrom the bullets behind the seats.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FAfterwards passengers escaped through
OL,18,Fan emergency exit and ran away with
OL,19,Fgunfire and explosions still going on
OL,20,Fin the plane, said Mr Thexton.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Some of the passengers who escaped
OL,6, through the siege plane's emergency
OL,7, exit are reported to have suffered
OL,8, broken limbs when they jumped off the
OL,9, wing.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FOne of the British passengers, Mr
OL,12,FHarish Parmat, told how one of the
OL,13,Fhijackers tried to escape by mingling
OL,14,Fwith the passengers as they ran away
OL,15,Ffrom the plane.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FBut passengers pointed at the man and
OL,18,Fsaid, "He's a terrorist", and police
OL,19,Farrested him, said Mr Parmat.
OL,20,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Another of the British passengers on
OL,6, the Karachi siege plane, Mr John
OL,7, Hussey, said it became extremely tense
OL,8, after the lights went out.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThen the leader of the hijackers could
OL,11,Fbe heard giving instructions in Arabic,
OL,12,Fand stationed men round the plane.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThere was a crack like that of a
OL,15,Fpercussion grenade and bursts of
OL,16,Fmachine-gun fire.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThen there was silence and passengers
OL,19,Fescaped through emergency hatches,
OL,20,Fafter which there was more firing, and
OL,21,Fpassengers ran away doubled up to the
OL,22,Fnearest shelter.
OL,23,T                     D]CFrom 06-09-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11811
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Moslem extremists posing as
OL,6, photographers are believed to have
OL,7, attacked a synagogue in Istanbul,
OL,8, killing 25 people and wounding seven.
OL,10,FSeveral men armed with machine-guns
OL,11,Fopened fire during Sabbath morning
OL,12,Fprayers.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FA local official said the attackers
OL,15,Falso set off an explosion that caused a
OL,16,Fhuge fire.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe Shi'ite Moslem organisation Islamic
OL,19,FJihad said it was responsible.
OL,20,F
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11812
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The leader of the SPLA rebel forces in
OL,6, southern Sudan, Col John Garang, has
OL,7, again threatened to shoot down planes
OL,8, flying over his territory without leave
OL,10,FHe expressed no regret for the shooting
OL,11,Fdown of a Sudan Airways plane with the
OL,12,Floss of 60 lives three weeks ago.
OL,14,FIn an interview inside Sudan with a BBC
OL,15,Fcorrespondent, Col Garang said the SPLA
OL,16,Fwere willing to discuss famine relief
OL,17,Ffor besieged government-held towns.
OL,19,FBut he said the problem of hunger in
OL,20,Frural areas controlled by the SPLA
OL,21,Foutweighed the problem in the towns.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11813
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1788696231
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Two women found dead in a blazing house
OL,6, in Birmingham had been strangled,
OL,7, police have said.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FA bloodstained man was also found in
OL,10,Fthe building and police were waiting
OL,11,Fat his bedside in the poisons unit at
OL,12,FDudley hospital to question him.
OL,14,FA police spokesman said no-one else
OL,15,Fwas being sought in connection with
OL,16,Fthe deaths at the house in Simmonds
OL,17,FDrive, Woodgate Valley.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FA number of children who were in the
OL,20,Fhouse were unhurt.
OL,21,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 06-09-86   teletextarchive.com
